IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ga-dates`

-- Guardianship Act 1987 (NSW) -- Part 5, medical and dental treatment (ss 32-48), from the seat of the patient.
--
-- SEAT: the patient of 16 or over who cannot consent to medical or dental treatment. Every exported question is one that
-- person (or someone asking on their behalf) would ask: "Does Part 5 apply to me?", "What kind of treatment is this?",
-- "Who is my person responsible?", "Who can consent for me?", "Can I be treated without anyone's consent?", "Does the
-- consent given for me count, if I object?", "Can the Tribunal consent?", "Was treating me an offence, and what is the
-- penalty?", "Can I still sue the practitioner?". The practitioner, the person responsible and the Tribunal get no seat.
--
-- ANSWERS. JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no; NOTHING, with a NOTHING-kind comment, where it does
-- not answer. The practitioner's and the Tribunal's judgments ("considers", "satisfied") are asked as facts. Treatment the
-- regulations declare major, special or excluded is asked as a fact: the Guardianship Regulation is not deposited.
--
-- Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website (as collected by the Open Australian Legal Corpus on
-- 10 March 2025; version as at 27 March 2021; unofficial, possibly out of date). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for
-- public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Guardianship Act 1987 -- Part 5 medical and dental treatment`

§§ `The nouns`

DECLARE `The kind of treatment` IS ONE OF
    `not medical or dental treatment for Part 5`
    `treatment in the course of a clinical trial`
    `special treatment`
    `major treatment`
    `minor treatment`

§§ `ss 33(2), 34(1) -- does Part 5 apply to me`

-- s 34(1) "This Part applies to a patient-- (a) who is of or above the age of 16 years, and (b) who is incapable of giving
-- consent to the carrying out of medical or dental treatment." s 33(2) "a person is incapable of giving consent ... if the
-- person-- (a) is incapable of understanding the general nature and effect of the proposed treatment, or (b) is incapable
-- of indicating whether or not he or she consents or does not consent". Outside s 34(1) (a scope limit with no "only")
-- the answer is NOTHING: the Part does not say what happens, and the patient's own consent or other law governs (fork
-- F12). s 34(2): the Mental Health Act 2007 and the Mental Health and Cognitive Impairment Forensic Provisions Act 2020
-- prevail where inconsistent (a comment).
@export Does Part 5 of the Guardianship Act (consent to medical and dental treatment for people who cannot consent) apply to me (ss 33(2), 34)?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the day of the proposed treatment` IS A DATE @desc The day the treatment would be carried out
      `I can understand the general nature and effect of the treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are capable of understanding the general nature and effect of the proposed treatment
      `I can indicate whether I consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are capable of indicating whether or not you consent to the treatment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does Part 5 apply to me` MEANS
    IF     (`born on` `my date of birth` `is at least` 16 `years old on` `the day of the proposed treatment`)
       AND ((NOT `I can understand the general nature and effect of the treatment`) OR (NOT `I can indicate whether I consent`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (a scope limit with no "only"; fork F12)

§§ `s 33(1) -- what kind of treatment`

-- s 33(1) "medical or dental treatment ... means-- (a) medical treatment (including any medical or surgical procedure,
-- operation or examination and any prophylactic, palliative or rehabilitative care) normally carried out by or under the
-- supervision of a medical practitioner, or (b) dental treatment ... normally carried out by or under the supervision of a
-- dentist, or (c) any other act declared by the regulations to be treatment ..., but does not include-- (d) any
-- non-intrusive examination made for diagnostic purposes ..., or (e) first-aid medical or dental treatment, or (f) the
-- administration of a pharmaceutical drug for the purpose, and in accordance with the dosage level, recommended in the
-- manufacturer's instructions (being a drug for which a prescription is not required and which is normally
-- self-administered), or (g) any other kind of treatment that is declared by the regulations not to be treatment".
-- "special treatment means-- (a) any treatment that is intended, or is reasonably likely, to have the effect of rendering
-- permanently infertile the person ..., or (b) any new treatment that has not yet gained the support of a substantial
-- number of medical practitioners or dentists specialising in the area of practice concerned, or (c) any other kind of
-- treatment declared by the regulations to be special treatment ..., but does not include treatment in the course of a
-- clinical trial." "major treatment means treatment (other than special treatment or treatment in the course of a
-- clinical trial) that is declared by the regulations to be major treatment". "minor treatment means treatment that is
-- not special treatment, major treatment or treatment in the course of a clinical trial." Every head is a "means".
GIVEN `it is medical or dental treatment normally given by or under a doctor or dentist, or declared treatment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is excluded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in the course of a clinical trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is intended or reasonably likely to make me permanently infertile` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is new and not yet supported by a substantial number of specialists` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulations declare it special treatment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulations declare it major treatment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The kind of treatment`
`the kind of treatment` `it is medical or dental treatment normally given by or under a doctor or dentist, or declared treatment` `it is excluded` `it is in the course of a clinical trial` `it is intended or reasonably likely to make me permanently infertile` `it is new and not yet supported by a substantial number of specialists` `the regulations declare it special treatment` `the regulations declare it major treatment` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `it is medical or dental treatment normally given by or under a doctor or dentist, or declared treatment`) THEN `not medical or dental treatment for Part 5`
           IF `it is excluded` THEN `not medical or dental treatment for Part 5`
           IF `it is in the course of a clinical trial` THEN `treatment in the course of a clinical trial`
           IF `it is intended or reasonably likely to make me permanently infertile` OR `it is new and not yet supported by a substantial number of specialists` OR `the regulations declare it special treatment` THEN `special treatment`
           IF `the regulations declare it major treatment` THEN `major treatment`
           OTHERWISE `minor treatment`

@export What kind of treatment is this under Part 5: special, major, minor, in a clinical trial, or not treatment at all (s 33(1))?
GIVEN `it is medical or dental treatment normally given by or under a doctor or dentist, or declared treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is medical treatment (a procedure, operation, examination, or preventive, palliative or rehabilitative care) normally carried out by or under a doctor, dental treatment normally carried out by or under a dentist, or an act the regulations declare to be treatment
      `it is a non-intrusive diagnostic examination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is only a non-intrusive examination for diagnosis (for example looking into the mouth, throat, nose, eyes or ears)
      `it is first aid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is first-aid medical or dental treatment
      `it is a non-prescription drug given as the maker recommends` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is giving a drug that needs no prescription and is normally self-administered, for the purpose and at the dose the manufacturer recommends
      `the regulations declare it not to be treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Guardianship Regulation declares this kind of treatment not to be treatment for Part 5
      `it is in the course of a clinical trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is given in the course of a clinical trial of drugs or techniques
      `it is intended or reasonably likely to make me permanently infertile` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is intended, or reasonably likely, to make you permanently infertile
      `it is new and not yet supported by a substantial number of specialists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a new treatment that has not yet gained the support of a substantial number of doctors or dentists specialising in that area
      `the regulations declare it special treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Guardianship Regulation declares it to be special treatment
      `the regulations declare it major treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Guardianship Regulation declares it to be major treatment (for example a general anaesthetic or certain long-acting drugs)
GIVETH A `The kind of treatment`
`What kind of treatment is this` MEANS
    `the kind of treatment` `it is medical or dental treatment normally given by or under a doctor or dentist, or declared treatment` `excluded` `it is in the course of a clinical trial` `it is intended or reasonably likely to make me permanently infertile` `it is new and not yet supported by a substantial number of specialists` `the regulations declare it special treatment` `the regulations declare it major treatment`
    WHERE
        `excluded` MEANS `it is a non-intrusive diagnostic examination` OR `it is first aid` OR `it is a non-prescription drug given as the maker recommends` OR `the regulations declare it not to be treatment`

§§ `s 33A -- who is my person responsible`

-- s 33A(2): for a child (under 18, s 3(1)), "the person having parental responsibility" (Children and Young Persons (Care
-- and Protection) Act 1998), or the Minister or the Secretary if the child is in their care. s 33A(3): for a person in the
-- Secretary's care under s 13, the Secretary. s 33A(4): otherwise, in descending order, "(a) the person's guardian, if
-- any, but only if the order or instrument appointing the guardian provides for the guardian to exercise the function of
-- giving consent to the carrying out of medical or dental treatment on the person, (b) the spouse of the person, if any,
-- if-- (i) the relationship between the person and the spouse is close and continuing, and (ii) the spouse is not a person
-- under guardianship, (c) a person who has the care of the person, (d) a close friend or relative of the person." s
-- 33A(5): a person who "declines in writing" or is certified in writing "not capable of carrying out those functions" is
-- passed over to "the person next in the hierarchy". "Guardian" includes an enduring guardian (s 3(1)). Where no one in
-- the hierarchy is left, the Act (s 37(2)(a)) speaks of there being "no person responsible".
DECLARE `My person responsible` IS ONE OF
    `the person with parental responsibility for me`
    `the Minister`
    `the Secretary`
    `my guardian`
    `my spouse`
    `the person who has the care of me`
    `my close friend or relative`
    `no one`

DECLARE `As a child I am in the care of` IS ONE OF
    `the Minister's care`
    `the Secretary's care`
    `neither's care`

@export Who is my "person responsible", who can consent to minor and major treatment for me (s 33A)?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the day of the proposed treatment` IS A DATE @desc The day the treatment would be carried out
      `as a child I am in the care of` IS A `As a child I am in the care of` @desc If you are under 18: whether you are in the care of the Minister or of the Secretary of the Department. One of: "the Minister's care", "the Secretary's care", "neither's care"
      `I am in the Secretary's care after being removed under section 11 or 12` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been removed from premises under the Act and placed in the care of the Secretary (s 13)
      `I have a guardian whose appointment covers consent to treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a guardian or enduring guardian whose order or appointment gives them the function of consenting to medical or dental treatment on you
      `my guardian has declined in writing or been certified incapable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that guardian has declined in writing to act as person responsible, or a doctor or other expert has certified in writing that they cannot
      `I have a spouse in a close and continuing relationship who is not under guardianship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a spouse or de facto partner (the last to qualify) whose relationship with you is close and continuing, and who is not themselves under guardianship
      `my spouse has declined in writing or been certified incapable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that spouse has declined in writing, or been certified in writing as not capable
      `someone has the care of me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone has the care of you (regularly provides or arranges domestic services and support, unpaid apart from a carer's pension)
      `my carer has declined in writing or been certified incapable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that carer has declined in writing, or been certified in writing as not capable
      `I have a close friend or relative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a close friend or relative (frequent personal contact, a close personal relationship and a personal interest in your welfare, and not paid for caring for you)
      `my close friend or relative has declined in writing or been certified incapable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that close friend or relative has declined in writing, or been certified in writing as not capable
GIVETH A `My person responsible`
`Who is my person responsible` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`born on` `my date of birth` `is at least` 18 `years old on` `the day of the proposed treatment`))
    THEN CONSIDER `as a child I am in the care of`
         WHEN `the Minister's care` THEN `the Minister`
         WHEN `the Secretary's care` THEN `the Secretary`
         OTHERWISE `the person with parental responsibility for me`
    ELSE BRANCH IF `I am in the Secretary's care after being removed under section 11 or 12` THEN `the Secretary`
                IF `I have a guardian whose appointment covers consent to treatment` AND (NOT `my guardian has declined in writing or been certified incapable`) THEN `my guardian`
                IF `I have a spouse in a close and continuing relationship who is not under guardianship` AND (NOT `my spouse has declined in writing or been certified incapable`) THEN `my spouse`
                IF `someone has the care of me` AND (NOT `my carer has declined in writing or been certified incapable`) THEN `the person who has the care of me`
                IF `I have a close friend or relative` AND (NOT `my close friend or relative has declined in writing or been certified incapable`) THEN `my close friend or relative`
                OTHERWISE `no one`

§§ `ss 36, 45A, 45AB -- who can consent for me`

-- s 36(1) "Consent ... may be given-- (a) in the case of minor or major treatment--by the person responsible for the
-- patient, or (b) in any case--by the Tribunal." s 36(2): the guardian may consent to continuing or further special
-- treatment if the Tribunal has consented to the treatment and authorised the guardian (s 45A). s 45AB(1)(a): for an
-- approved clinical trial the Tribunal may determine that persons responsible give or withhold consent (Division 3).
DECLARE `Who can consent for me` IS ONE OF
    `Part 5 does not require consent to this`
    `my person responsible or the Tribunal`
    `only the Tribunal, as I have no person responsible`
    `only the Tribunal`
    `the Tribunal, or my guardian under the Tribunal's authority`

@export Who can consent to this treatment on me (ss 36, 45A, 45AB)?
GIVEN `the kind of treatment` IS A `The kind of treatment` @desc The kind of treatment (see the question on the kind of treatment). One of: "not medical or dental treatment for Part 5", "treatment in the course of a clinical trial", "special treatment", "major treatment", "minor treatment"
      `I have a person responsible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a person responsible (see the question on who is your person responsible)
      `my guardian has the Tribunal's authority for continuing or further special treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For special treatment: whether the Tribunal has consented to this treatment before and authorised your guardian to consent to its continuation or to further treatment of a similar nature
      `the Tribunal has let persons responsible consent for this trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a clinical trial: whether the Tribunal has determined that persons responsible are to give or withhold consent for patients in this trial
GIVETH A `Who can consent for me`
`Who can consent to my treatment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of treatment`
    WHEN `not medical or dental treatment for Part 5` THEN `Part 5 does not require consent to this`
    WHEN `special treatment` THEN
        IF `my guardian has the Tribunal's authority for continuing or further special treatment`
        THEN `the Tribunal, or my guardian under the Tribunal's authority`
        ELSE `only the Tribunal`
    WHEN `treatment in the course of a clinical trial` THEN
        IF `the Tribunal has let persons responsible consent for this trial` AND `I have a person responsible`
        THEN `my person responsible or the Tribunal`
        ELSE `only the Tribunal`
    OTHERWISE
        IF `I have a person responsible`
        THEN `my person responsible or the Tribunal`
        ELSE `only the Tribunal, as I have no person responsible`

§§ `s 37 -- treatment without consent`

-- s 37(1) "Medical or dental treatment may be carried out on a patient to whom this Part applies without consent ... if
-- the medical practitioner or dentist carrying out or supervising the treatment considers the treatment is necessary, as a
-- matter of urgency-- (a) to save the patient's life, or (b) to prevent serious damage to the patient's health, or (c)
-- except in the case of special treatment--to prevent the patient from suffering or continuing to suffer significant pain
-- or distress." s 37(2) "Minor treatment may (subject to subsection (3)) also be carried out ... without any consent ... if--
-- (a) there is no person responsible for the patient, or (b) there is such a person but that person either cannot be
-- contacted or is unable or unwilling to make a decision". s 37(3): the practitioner "is required to certify in writing in
-- the patient's clinical record that-- (a) the treatment is necessary and is the form of treatment that will most
-- successfully promote the patient's health and well-being, and (b) the patient does not object". The certificate is read
-- as a condition of s 37(2) ("subject to subsection (3)") (fork F13). A failed "if" is JUST FALSE.
DECLARE `The urgency` IS ONE OF
    `to save my life`
    `to prevent serious damage to my health`
    `to prevent significant pain or distress`
    `it is not urgent`

@export Can this treatment be carried out on me without anyone's consent (s 37)?
GIVEN `the kind of treatment` IS A `The kind of treatment` @desc The kind of treatment. One of: "not medical or dental treatment for Part 5", "treatment in the course of a clinical trial", "special treatment", "major treatment", "minor treatment"
      `the practitioner considers it urgently necessary` IS A `The urgency` @desc What the doctor or dentist carrying out or supervising the treatment considers it is urgently necessary for. One of: "to save my life", "to prevent serious damage to my health", "to prevent significant pain or distress", "it is not urgent"
      `I have a person responsible who can be contacted and will decide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a person responsible who can be contacted and is able and willing to make a decision about consent
      `the practitioner certified the treatment necessary and best, and that I do not object` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For minor treatment: whether the doctor or dentist certified in writing in your clinical record that the treatment is necessary and the form of treatment that will most successfully promote your health and well-being, and that you do not object
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I be treated without consent` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of treatment`
    WHEN `not medical or dental treatment for Part 5` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (Part 5 does not regulate it)
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `the practitioner considers it urgently necessary`
        WHEN `to save my life` THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 37(1)(a)
        WHEN `to prevent serious damage to my health` THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 37(1)(b)
        WHEN `to prevent significant pain or distress` THEN
            IF `special` THEN `the minor treatment route` ELSE JUST TRUE  -- s 37(1)(c) "except in the case of special treatment"
        OTHERWISE `the minor treatment route`
    WHERE
        `special` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the kind of treatment`
            WHEN `special treatment` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `minor` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the kind of treatment`
            WHEN `minor treatment` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `the minor treatment route` MEANS
            IF `minor` AND (NOT `I have a person responsible who can be contacted and will decide`) AND `the practitioner certified the treatment necessary and best, and that I do not object`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 37(2), (3)
            ELSE JUST FALSE  -- s 37(1), (2) "if"

§§ `ss 33(3), 46, 46A -- does the consent given for me count`

-- s 33(3) "a person shall be taken to object ...-- (a) if the person indicates (by whatever means) that he or she does not
-- want the treatment to be carried out, or (b) if the person-- (i) has previously indicated, in similar circumstances,
-- that he or she did not then want the treatment to be carried out, and (ii) has not subsequently indicated to the
-- contrary." s 46(1): a consent has effect as if the patient had been capable and had consented. s 46(2) "A consent given by
-- a person responsible for, or the guardian of, the patient has no effect-- (a) if the person carrying out or supervising
-- the proposed treatment is aware, or ought reasonably to be aware, that the patient objects ..., or (b) if the proposed
-- treatment is to be carried out for any purpose other than that of promoting or maintaining the health and well-being of
-- the patient." s 46(3): a guardian's consent has effect despite an objection if given under the Tribunal's s 46A
-- authority (which covers major or minor treatment only, s 46A(1), and may be used only if the guardian is satisfied the
-- treatment is manifestly in the patient's best interests, s 46A(4)). s 46(4): an objection "is to be disregarded if-- (a)
-- the patient has minimal or no understanding of what the treatment entails, and (b) the treatment will cause the patient
-- no distress or, if it will cause the patient some distress, the distress is likely to be reasonably tolerable and only
-- transitory." A Tribunal consent is outside s 46(2).
DECLARE `Who consented` IS ONE OF
    `my person responsible gave it`
    `my guardian gave it`
    `the Tribunal gave it`

@export Does the consent given for my treatment have effect, given what I have said about it (ss 33(3), 46, 46A)?
GIVEN `who consented` IS A `Who consented` @desc Who gave the consent. One of: "my person responsible gave it", "my guardian gave it", "the Tribunal gave it"
      `the kind of treatment` IS A `The kind of treatment` @desc The kind of treatment. One of: "not medical or dental treatment for Part 5", "treatment in the course of a clinical trial", "special treatment", "major treatment", "minor treatment"
      `I have indicated that I do not want it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have indicated, by any means, that you do not want the treatment
      `I said no before in similar circumstances and have not said otherwise since` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you previously indicated, in similar circumstances, that you did not want the treatment, and have not since indicated otherwise
      `the practitioner knows or ought reasonably to know I object` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person carrying out or supervising the treatment is aware, or ought reasonably to be aware, that you object
      `I have minimal or no understanding of what it entails` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have minimal or no understanding of what the treatment entails
      `it will cause me no distress, or only tolerable and transitory distress` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the treatment will cause you no distress, or only distress likely to be reasonably tolerable and only transitory
      `it is for promoting or maintaining my health and well-being` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the treatment is to be carried out to promote or maintain your health and well-being (and not for another purpose)
      `my guardian has the Tribunal's authority to override my objection and uses it in my manifest best interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has authorised your guardian (s 46A) to override your objection and the guardian is satisfied the treatment is manifestly in your best interests
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does the consent given for me have effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who consented`
    WHEN `the Tribunal gave it` THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 46(1); s 46(2) does not reach the Tribunal's consent
    OTHERWISE
        BRANCH IF (NOT `it is for promoting or maintaining my health and well-being`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 46(2)(b) "has no effect"
               IF `guardian override` THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 46(3), 46A
               IF `an objection that counts` AND `the practitioner knows or ought reasonably to know I object` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 46(2)(a) "has no effect"
               OTHERWISE JUST TRUE  -- s 46(1)
    WHERE
        `I object` MEANS `I have indicated that I do not want it` OR `I said no before in similar circumstances and have not said otherwise since`
        `the objection is disregarded` MEANS `I have minimal or no understanding of what it entails` AND `it will cause me no distress, or only tolerable and transitory distress`
        `an objection that counts` MEANS `I object` AND (NOT `the objection is disregarded`)
        `major or minor` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the kind of treatment`
            WHEN `major treatment` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `minor treatment` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `guardian override` MEANS
            CONSIDER `who consented`
            WHEN `my guardian gave it` THEN `major or minor` AND `my guardian has the Tribunal's authority to override my objection and uses it in my manifest best interests`
            OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `ss 44, 45, 45AA -- can the Tribunal consent`

-- s 44(1) "If, after conducting a hearing ..., the Tribunal is satisfied that it is appropriate for the treatment to be
-- carried out, it may consent". s 45(1) "The Tribunal must not give consent ... unless the Tribunal is satisfied that the
-- treatment is the most appropriate form of treatment for promoting and maintaining the patient's health and well-being."
-- s 45(2) "However, the Tribunal must not give consent to the carrying out of special treatment unless it is satisfied
-- that the treatment is necessary-- (a) to save the patient's life, or (b) to prevent serious damage to the patient's
-- health, or unless the Tribunal is authorised to give that consent under subsection (3)." s 45(3): for new special
-- treatment (para (b) of the definition) or prescribed special treatment other than sterilising treatment, the Tribunal
-- may consent if satisfied "(c) the treatment is the only or most appropriate way of treating the patient and is manifestly
-- in the best interests of the patient, and (d) ... [relevant NHMRC guidelines] have been or will be complied with".
-- s 45AA(4): for a clinical trial, the Tribunal must first have approved the trial; without approval the Act does not say
-- the Tribunal cannot consent to treatment in it (NOTHING; fork F15).
@export Can the Tribunal consent to this treatment on me (ss 44(1), 45, 45AA)?
GIVEN `the kind of treatment` IS A `The kind of treatment` @desc The kind of treatment. One of: "not medical or dental treatment for Part 5", "treatment in the course of a clinical trial", "special treatment", "major treatment", "minor treatment"
      `the Tribunal held a hearing and is satisfied the treatment is appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, after a hearing, the Tribunal is satisfied that it is appropriate for the treatment to be carried out
      `the Tribunal is satisfied it is the most appropriate treatment for my health and well-being` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal is satisfied that the treatment is the most appropriate form of treatment for promoting and maintaining your health and well-being
      `the Tribunal is satisfied it is necessary to save my life or prevent serious damage to my health` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For special treatment: whether the Tribunal is satisfied it is necessary to save your life or to prevent serious damage to your health
      `it is new special treatment, or prescribed special treatment that is not sterilising` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For special treatment: whether it is special because it is new and not yet widely supported, or because the regulations prescribe it (and it is not treatment intended or likely to make you permanently infertile)
      `the Tribunal is satisfied it is the only or most appropriate way and manifestly in my best interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For such special treatment: whether the Tribunal is satisfied it is the only or most appropriate way of treating you and manifestly in your best interests
      `relevant NHMRC guidelines have been or will be complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For such special treatment: whether any relevant National Health and Medical Research Council guidelines have been or will be complied with (answer yes if there are none)
      `the Tribunal has approved the clinical trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For treatment in a clinical trial: whether the Tribunal has approved the trial under s 45AA
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Tribunal consent to my treatment` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `not treatment` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (Part 5 does not regulate it; s 46(5) lets consent be given anyway)
           IF `trial` AND (NOT `the Tribunal has approved the clinical trial`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (fork F15)
           IF (NOT `the Tribunal held a hearing and is satisfied the treatment is appropriate`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 44(1) "If ... satisfied"
           IF (NOT `the Tribunal is satisfied it is the most appropriate treatment for my health and well-being`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 45(1) "must not ... unless"
           IF `special` THEN
               IF     `the Tribunal is satisfied it is necessary to save my life or prevent serious damage to my health`
                   OR (    `it is new special treatment, or prescribed special treatment that is not sterilising`
                       AND `the Tribunal is satisfied it is the only or most appropriate way and manifestly in my best interests`
                       AND `relevant NHMRC guidelines have been or will be complied with`)
               THEN JUST TRUE
               ELSE JUST FALSE  -- s 45(2) "must not ... unless"
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `not treatment` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the kind of treatment`
            WHEN `not medical or dental treatment for Part 5` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `trial` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the kind of treatment`
            WHEN `treatment in the course of a clinical trial` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `special` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the kind of treatment`
            WHEN `special treatment` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `ss 35, 106 -- was treating me an offence, and the penalty`

-- s 35(1) "A person must not carry out medical or dental treatment on a patient to whom this Part applies unless-- (a)
-- consent for the treatment has been given in accordance with this Part, or (b) the carrying out of the treatment is
-- authorised by this Part without any such consent, or (c) the treatment is carried out in accordance with an order made
-- by the Supreme Court in the exercise of its jurisdiction with respect to the guardianship of persons." s 35(1A): (c) does
-- not apply to sterilising special treatment or special treatment prescribed for that subsection. s 35(2): the section
-- does not limit any other law under which minor treatment may be given without consent. Once an "unless" is met there is
-- no offence (JUST FALSE; fork F14). Whether consent was given "in accordance with this Part" and whether a
-- treatment was "authorised" are asked: the other questions here help to answer them.
@export Was carrying out this treatment on me an offence under section 35?
GIVEN `Part 5 applied to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Part 5 applied to you (16 or older, and unable to understand the treatment's nature and effect or to indicate consent)
      `the kind of treatment` IS A `The kind of treatment` @desc The kind of treatment. One of: "not medical or dental treatment for Part 5", "treatment in the course of a clinical trial", "special treatment", "major treatment", "minor treatment"
      `consent was given in accordance with Part 5` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether consent was given by someone entitled under Part 5 (your person responsible, your guardian or the Tribunal) and had effect
      `Part 5 authorised it without consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Part 5 authorised the treatment without consent (for example urgent treatment to save your life)
      `it was under a Supreme Court guardianship order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the treatment was carried out in accordance with an order of the Supreme Court in its guardianship jurisdiction
      `it is sterilising or prescribed for section 35(1A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is special treatment intended or reasonably likely to make you permanently infertile, or special treatment the regulations prescribe for s 35(1A)
      `another law allowed this minor treatment without my consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For minor treatment: whether another Act or law allowed it to be carried out without your consent
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was treating me an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `Part 5 applied to me`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 35 reaches only a patient to whom Part 5 applies)
           IF `not treatment` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (outside the definition of treatment in s 33(1))
           IF `consent was given in accordance with Part 5` OR `Part 5 authorised it without consent` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 35(1)(a), (b) (fork F14)
           IF `it was under a Supreme Court guardianship order` AND (NOT `it is sterilising or prescribed for section 35(1A)`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 35(1)(c), (1A)
           IF `minor` AND `another law allowed this minor treatment without my consent` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 35(2)
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE  -- s 35(1) "must not ... unless"
    WHERE
        `not treatment` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the kind of treatment`
            WHEN `not medical or dental treatment for Part 5` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `minor` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the kind of treatment`
            WHEN `minor treatment` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 35(1) "Maximum penalty-- in the case of special treatment or treatment in the course of a clinical trial (on conviction
-- on indictment)--imprisonment for 7 years, or in the case of minor or major treatment (on summary conviction)--
-- imprisonment for 1 year or 10 penalty units, or both." s 106(2): s 35(1) offences are dealt with on indictment, which
-- does not sit easily with "on summary conviction" for minor or major treatment (finding 5). The text sets no fine for
-- special treatment: NOTHING. A penalty unit's value is in the Crimes (Sentencing Procedure) Act 1999, s 17 (not
-- deposited).
@export What is the longest imprisonment, in years, for unlawfully carrying out this kind of treatment on me (s 35(1))?
GIVEN `the kind of treatment` IS A `The kind of treatment` @desc The kind of treatment. One of: "not medical or dental treatment for Part 5", "treatment in the course of a clinical trial", "special treatment", "major treatment", "minor treatment"
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`The longest imprisonment for unlawful treatment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of treatment`
    WHEN `not medical or dental treatment for Part 5` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (outside s 35)
    WHEN `special treatment` THEN JUST 7
    WHEN `treatment in the course of a clinical trial` THEN JUST 7
    OTHERWISE JUST 1

@export What is the largest fine, in penalty units, for unlawfully carrying out this kind of treatment on me (s 35(1))?
GIVEN `the kind of treatment` IS A `The kind of treatment` @desc The kind of treatment. One of: "not medical or dental treatment for Part 5", "treatment in the course of a clinical trial", "special treatment", "major treatment", "minor treatment"
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`The largest fine for unlawful treatment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of treatment`
    WHEN `major treatment` THEN JUST 10
    WHEN `minor treatment` THEN JUST 10
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (the text sets no fine for special or clinical-trial treatment, and none outside s 35)

§§ `ss 46(1), 47 -- can I still sue for the treatment`

-- s 46(1): a consent under Part 5 has effect as if the patient had been capable of consenting and the treatment had been
-- carried out with the patient's consent. s 47 "Nothing in this Part relieves a person from liability in respect of the
-- carrying out of medical or dental treatment on a patient to whom this Part applies, being a liability to which the person
-- would have been subject-- (a) had the patient been capable of giving consent ..., and (b) had the treatment been carried
-- out with the patient's consent." So a claim (for example in negligence) that would lie against a consenting patient's
-- practitioner still lies; Part 5 creates no new one. Whether the practitioner would be liable is the general law's
-- question, asked.
@export I was treated under a Part 5 consent: can I still hold the practitioner liable as I could have had I consented myself (ss 46(1), 47)?
GIVEN `the practitioner would be liable had I been able to consent and consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, under the general law (for example negligence), the person who carried out the treatment would be liable to you for it if you had been capable of consenting and had consented
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I still hold the practitioner liable` MEANS
    IF `the practitioner would be liable had I been able to consent and consented`
    THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 47 "Nothing in this Part relieves a person from liability"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 47 preserves liability; it does not create any; the general law decides)
